config RV_MON_OOB_TRAP
	depends on RV
	depends on RV_MON_DOVETAIL
	default y
	select HA_MON_EVENTS_ID
	bool "oob_trap monitor"
	help
	  Per-task monitor checking the Dovetail trap contract: every
	  exception the arch code must notify, taken out-of-band, is notified
	  with its trap number, every notification is unwound once for the
	  same trap, the trap exit handler returns with hard irqs off, a
	  kernel mode exception over a context with hard irqs off keeps them
	  off, no task is demoted from interrupt or NMI context, no task
	  schedules out while a kprobe is being handled, and every trap ends
	  within timeout_ms. With EVL, a kernel mode trap must also end on
	  the stage it was notified from, and the task must be demoted for
	  every user mode trap.

	  For further information, see:
	    Documentation/trace/rv/monitor_dovetail.rst
